                <pb facs="0584" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/694: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-14T18:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Although it is understood that the Greek Government is tendering payment of
                    35 percent of the face value of the coupons falling due from time to time on its
                    foreign loans, this Government has received no payment on the amounts due May 10
                    under Part II of the Debt Agreement of May 10, 1929, and has received no
                    communication from the Greek Government regarding them.</p>
                <p>If you perceive no objection, please inquire confidentially and informally of the
                    International Financial Commission as to its action with reference to this
                    situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
